  "interpretation": "Scope: the frozen six known loadouts in this roster, with uncertainty only over the legal unseen third selection. All alternatives replay the entire prefix with identical public logs. Common side-one witnesses choose Psychic first and consult only own HP/status/PP, visible opponent species and public living count. Each lower bound allows a full-information opponent to optimize every action. The side-zero witnesses give upper bounds even to a type-informed side one. Weighted common-policy lower bounds and weighted type-informed upper bounds therefore bracket the value for a declared type distribution; equal weights describe the current conditional selection model, not an empirical or optimal opponent prior. Minimum bounds cover adversarial type selection. Cloyster-only recovery raises the guaranteed score against a full-information opponent relative to the always-attack witness; it is not a comparison to the deployed search bot. First-Psychic regret upper bounds permit optimal subsequent public play and do not certify the deployed continuation policy. The game-value intervals remain unresolved. No full-game ceiling, human calibration or deployed strength gain is established."
